; tests/gen-query-flow-find-band.fk — the FIND lane of the generated queries.
;
; The find lane runs on Go, Rust AND TypeScript. It did not when it was written:
; a find query returns a node id above 2^31 and the TS arm truncated it, so this
; band was first declared "GO AND RUST ONLY" on the strength of a `| 0` in
; compiler.ts and a comment about SMI tagging. That reading was wrong. The loss
; was in kernel.ts internTrivialInt, which had no overflow branch where Go and
; Rust both do; it is fixed, and the lane is not a lane.
;
; preludes: form-stdlib/core.fk cognition/language-neutral-symbol-identity.fk cognition/steiner-neutral-kernel.fk cognition/gen-neutral-code.fk cognition/gen-query-flow.fk cognition/gen-query-walk.fk
;
; Verdict 3 on Go / Rust / TypeScript:
;   all four find questions agree with the hand-written accessor, on the
;     real graph, including the one with NO answer                       1
;   and a returned node id really is above 2^31 — the value this lane
;     exists to carry, stated so the constraint cannot be forgotten      2
(do
    (gqy-check-find))
